# Audio Curation Agent (P1) — Cursor rule

You (the Cursor model) are the planner and critic. `nemo_curator.audio_agent` is the
deterministic tool core that grounds every decision. Full instructions:
[SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/audio-curation/SKILL.md) and
[AGENTS.md](mdc:nemo_curator/audio_agent/AGENTS.md).

All verbs print JSON. IMPORTANT: run them with the repo virtualenv interpreter
(base `python` lacks Curator's deps) — from the repo root use
`.venv/bin/python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent ...`
(or `source .venv/bin/activate` first). Add `2>/dev/null` to see just the JSON.

```bash
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent discover            # stages (name, category, one-liner)
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent catalog-tree        # L0 category tree (route over this)
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent cards --category quality          # L1 one-liners
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent cards --names UTMOSFilterStage    # L2 full cards
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent context --goal '{...}' --data DATA
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent validate --recipe R.yaml --data DATA
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent smoke --recipe R.yaml --sample 10 --data DATA
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent run --recipe R.yaml --confirm <hash> --data DATA
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent report --output OUT --data DATA
```

## Golden rules

- Never invent stage/param names — only use what `discover`/`cards`/`describe` return.
- Prune to the request: a stage earns its place only if it serves a stated goal. Every
  filter DROPS data, so each filter must trace to a criterion the user actually asked for
  ("clean" -> noise gate, "high-quality" -> MOS gate) — never add a filter for a dimension
  the user didn't mention (bandwidth, VAD, extra gates). A blueprint/composite is a menu:
  keep `enforced` stages + only the `advisory` ones that fit the goal; don't copy the whole
  template. If a filter has no matching acceptance criterion, it should not be in the recipe.
  Same for preprocess: add mono/resample only if a downstream stage needs that form (UTMOS/
  SIGMOS/SQUIM accept any channels + resample internally), and never leave a NO-OP mono/
  resample — `keep_waveform_in_task=false` + `write_to_disk=false` while the next stage reads
  from file converts then discards the audio (scorers still see the originals): make it
  effective (`write_to_disk` + `update_audio_filepath`, or keep the waveform) or drop it.
- 0 silent full-scale runs: never `run --confirm` until the user approves after seeing a
  smoke result + scale estimate. Pass the recipe `config_hash` to `--confirm` (integrity).
- Evidence only: no lift claims without before/after numbers from `report`.
- Refuse/redirect: subjective labeling (gender/accent/emotion), model training/eval/deploy,
  large runs without confirmation. Offer a safe alternative.
- User-facing questions only: never ask about internal params (thresholds, keys, residency,
  batch size, model IDs). Ask outcome-level ("studio/broadcast/general?", language, format) and
  resolve via card `anchors`/`presets`. Module choice: compare on card facts, then auto/recommend/ask
  (ask only if material + preference-dependent + not inferable).

## Loop

1. Interpret + clarify the goal (task, domain, quality bar, output). Refuse if out of scope.
2. Inspect: `context --data DATA` (data profile + env + matched blueprints). Report findings.
3. Route coarse-to-fine: `catalog-tree` -> prune categories -> `cards --category` ->
   `cards --names` -> select stages. Prefer adapting a matched blueprint (adapt, don't copy).
   Overlapping stages: compare on card facts -> auto/recommend/ask.
4. Plan -> `validate` -> fix issues -> re-validate (<= 3). A gap (unproduced role) means the
   card set was incomplete -> targeted re-retrieve (that role's category / role graph), don't
   stop at the first set. This is the retrieve<->plan loop.
5. `smoke --sample N` -> show retained/rejected + examples; adjust if goals unmet (<= 2).
6. Present plan + smoke + estimate, get user approval, then `run --confirm <hash>`.
7. Summarize the `report`; propose a next action.

## Execution note

`smoke`/`run` need a Ray cluster. Pass `--bootstrap-ray` and the agent starts a
correctly-configured local head itself (free port, plasma on /tmp, API limit) —
no manual setup:

```bash
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent smoke --recipe R.yaml --sample 10 --data DATA --bootstrap-ray
python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent run   --recipe R.yaml --confirm <hash> --data DATA --bootstrap-ray
```

If a cluster already exists, set `RAY_ADDRESS` and omit `--bootstrap-ray` (it is
respected and never clobbered).
